<title>USA: JP Foodservice, Rykoff set $1.4 billion merger.</title>
<headline>JP Foodservice, Rykoff set $1.4 billion merger.</headline>
<dateline>COLUMBIA, Md. 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>JP Foodservice Inc. has agreed to acquire Rykoff-Sexton Inc. in a deal worth $1.4 billion, creating a food-service giant with annual sales of $5.2 billion, the companies said on Monday.</p>
<p>Together, the companies will have nationwide distribution capabilities and a customer base of more than 130,000 hotel, restaurant and institutional foodservice customers.</p>
</text>
